# What this repo tracks: the schemas, the NDJSON catalogues the DB is built from,
# the validation scripts + their tests, and the docs for those three. Everything
# else — sourcing/scraping/repair campaign tooling, audits, staging dumps, scratch
# files — lives here on disk but is NEVER committed. The rules below are an
# allowlist, not a blocklist: a new file is ignored unless it is one of those four.

# ── data/ — only the live catalogues, plus exactly ONE quarantine file ─────────
/data/*
!/data/fabricated_denylist.ndjson
!/data/analog_ics.ndjson
!/data/bjts.ndjson
!/data/capacitors.ndjson
!/data/circuits.ndjson
!/data/connectors.ndjson
!/data/controllers.ndjson
!/data/converters.ndjson
!/data/diodes.ndjson
!/data/igbts.ndjson
!/data/magnetics.ndjson
!/data/mosfets.ndjson
!/data/resistors.ndjson
!/data/thermistors.ndjson
!/data/timing_devices.ndjson
!/data/varistors.ndjson
# The single consolidated quarantine sink. Per-catalogue quarantine files
# (*.quarantine_*.ndjson), backups, vendor dumps and staging live local-only.
!/data/quarantine.ndjson

# ── scripts/ — only the validation entry points ───────────────────────────────
# Everything else in scripts/ is one-off ETL: vendor scraping/import, data repair,
# recovery, schema-migration campaigns. Historical tooling, not a library.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/validate_topology.py
!/scripts/validate_db.py
!/scripts/check_component_uris.py
!/scripts/check_no_fabricated_parts.py
!/scripts/verify_provenance_content.py
!/scripts/changed_records_gate.py
!/scripts/blade_gate.py
# The six per-catalogue audits (identity, units, cohorts, citations,
# verification, coverage) as arithmetic. It is a standing guard wired into
# integrity_scan.py, and a guard that is not in a fresh clone does not exist --
# which is exactly why the provenance cleanup could not be re-run.
!/scripts/catalogue_audit.py
!/scripts/integrity_scan.py
# A guard since it grew --check: provenance in a live catalogue is a reference, not
# an essay, and a one-shot cleanup nobody can run again does not hold that.
!/scripts/strip_provenance_narrative.py
# ABT #1082: a stored family must agree with the vendor's own Series for the
# exact order code. The one-shot repair of the 404 wrong WE-MAPI rows cannot
# hold that invariant against the next import; this can, repeatedly.
!/scripts/check_wurth_family_matches_series.py
# ABT #1090 (and #286, #431): an importer with no value for a field must omit
# it, never mint a constant. Catches a cohort sharing a byte-identical value
# that the parts' own descriptions refute.
!/scripts/check_no_constant_cohorts.py
# Retired on purpose: tests/test_no_fabricated_parts.py asserts it refuses to run.
!/scripts/backfill_provenance.py

# ── importers that write the catalogue ────────────────────────────────────────
# Tracked as of 2026-09-05. These are not one-off ETL: they are the code that
# PRODUCES catalogue rows, and every large defect cohort found in the 2026-09-05
# audit came from an importer, not from a thousand independently bad rows --
# 549 TDK chip beads minted an identical 1e-09 H, 404 Wuerth rows took a
# "WE-MAPI" default, 716 onsemi diodes were all called "rectifier". Their fixes
# living only on one machine is the same failure that left
# strip_provenance_narrative.py unrunnable by the next campaign.
# The gate those importers now call BEFORE a row may enter a catalogue: identity,
# citation, minted constant, arithmetic ladder, SI/possible units, schema (with
# required-but-vacuous counted as missing). An importer that imports it must find
# it in a fresh clone, and a gate nobody can run is not a gate.
!/scripts/ingest_gate.py
!/scripts/we_inductors_import.py
!/scripts/we_transformers_import.py
!/scripts/tdk_meister_import.py

# ── the standing integrity watchdog (cron 02:00) ─────────────────────────────
# Runs every guard nightly and reports only what is NEW. Costs zero model tokens:
# the expensive judgement was spent once, when each guard was written and
# counter-checked; running them is arithmetic.
!/scripts/integrity_scan.py
!/scripts/quarantine_recover.py
!/scripts/run_integrity_nightly.sh

# ── validator/ — the C++ Blade Runner sources, not its campaign drivers ───────
/validator/*.py
/validator/build*/

# ── local-only trees ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/staging/
# librarian/ — local-only missing-field enrichment system (Postgres-backed ticket
# queue + nightly DigiKey/Mouser+Sonnet loop). Runs only on this machine.
/librarian/
/backups/
.playwright-mcp/
.pytest_cache/

# ── loose scratch at the repo root ────────────────────────────────────────────
/*.py
/*.json
/*.ndjson
/*.csv
/*.txt

# ── scratch/temp everywhere ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.backup
*_pre_excel*
*.ndjson.tmp
__pycache__/
*.pyc
